{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/girvanNewmanCommunities()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"girvanNewmanCommunities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:18CommunityDetection20GirvanNewmanSequenceV","text":"GirvanNewmanSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GirvanNewmanSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The partitions, coarsest first: each time the number of components grows, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components; ending with every vertex alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m) to start. Each removal recomputes the betweenness of the removed edge’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component C alone, O(n_C · m_C); every split builds a partition in O(n). The whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence is O(m² n) in the worst case."}]}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Girvan–Newman communities: the successively finer partitions found by removing, again and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, the edge of greatest betweenness ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeBetweennessCentrality()"},{"type":"text","text":"), recomputed after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each removal. A tie goes to the least edge position; parallel copies share their pairs’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths, and self-loops are never removed and never matter. The sequence is lazy: each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition is computed when iteration reaches it."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/communitydetection\/graphprotocols\/graph\/girvannewmancommunities()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/CommunityDetection\/GirvanNewman.swift#L264","fileName":"GirvanNewman.swift"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"girvanNewmanCommunities()","modules":[{"name":"CommunityDetection","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"girvanNewmanCommunities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GirvanNewmanSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:18CommunityDetection20GirvanNewmanSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P18CommunityDetectionE23girvanNewmanCommunitiesAD06GirvanF8SequenceVyxGyF"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://CommunityDetection/documentation/CommunityDetection/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text